    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "what you’re looking at are Prometheus scrape duration metrics for your two exporters, plotted in Grafana. Each line in that legend corresponds to how long the exporter takes to collect and expose metrics when Prometheus scrapes it:\n\nslurm-exporter: job scrape (green)\nAverage scrape time of the cluster-wide Slurm exporter when it runs the Slurm commands (scontrol, sinfo, etc.) to gather job-related metrics.\n\nslurm-exporter: node scrape (yellow)\nAverage scrape time for the same exporter when it collects node-level metrics (CPU/memory per node, node states, etc.).\n\njob-exporter: avg scrape (5m) (blue)\nRolling 5-minute average scrape duration from the slurm-job-exporter (the custom exporter you added). This one specifically calls squeue and sacct to break down jobs by state, partition, user, and account.\n\n🔎 Why this matters:\n\nNormally scrape durations should be a fraction of a second (e.g. 0.1–2s).\n\nIf you see spikes into multiple seconds (or worse, >10s), Prometheus scrapes might timeout or skip samples, causing missing data in Grafana.\n\nLong scrape times usually mean the exporter is running expensive Slurm commands (like sacct) too frequently, or the cluster itself is slow to respond.\n\n✅ Rule of thumb:\n\nKeep scrape times < 5s (ideally < 1s).\n\nIf the job-exporter line is consistently higher, you might want to reduce the frequency of sacct calls or configure the scrape interval to be longer (e.g., 1m instead of 15s).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisCenteredZero": false,
            "axisColorMode": "text",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "barAlignment": 0,
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            },
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "pointSize": 5,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "group": "A",
              "mode": "none"
            },
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          },
          "decimals": 2,
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 80
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 11,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      },
      "id": 10,
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "calcs": [],
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "none"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "$datasource"
          },
          "expr": "avg(slurm_job_scrape_duration) without (container,instance,endpoint,pod,service,namespace)",
          "legendFormat": "slurm-exporter: job scrape",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "$datasource"
          },
          "expr": "avg(slurm_node_scrape_duration) without (container,instance,endpoint,pod,service,namespace)",
          "legendFormat": "slurm-exporter: node scrape",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "$datasource"
          },
          "expr": "rate(slurm_job_exporter_scrape_seconds_sum[5m]) / rate(slurm_job_exporter_scrape_seconds_count[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "job-exporter: avg scrape (5m)",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "title": "Exporter Scrape Durations",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "The State Snapshot (Latest) panel in your dashboard is essentially a table view of the most recent Slurm cluster state, pulled directly from the last scrape of your exporters.\n\nSpecifically, it is aggregating metrics like:\n\nCPU load, total, idle (slurm_cpu_load, slurm_cpus_total, slurm_cpus_idle)\n\nMemory real, allocated (slurm_mem_real, slurm_mem_alloc)\n\nCPUs per state (slurm_cpus_per_state{state=\"idle|mixed|alloc\"})\n\nJobs total (slurm_job_count_total or per-state)\n\nand presenting them in a table, so you get a point-in-time snapshot of the cluster without having to interpret time-series graphs.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "displayMode": "auto",
            "inspect": false
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 80
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "none"
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
